WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.240
In 1999, Darth Maul took the world by storm
with his brief appearance in Star Wars: The

00:00:05.241 --> 00:00:06.241
Phantom Menace.

00:00:06.241 --> 00:00:09.630
Though the movie's not really well-loved by
fans today, if there's one good thing that

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:12.480
came out of the first Star Wars prequel, it's
Darth Maul.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:17.470
Too bad he died at the end of the movie — or
did he, don don don ? Turns out getting chopped

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:21.570
in half and thrown down an elevator shaft
isn't quite the death sentence it used to

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:22.570
be.

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:24.660
Here's the untold truth of Darth Maul.

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:25.660
Planet of the Rancors

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:30.890
Remember the Rancor, the toothy, drooly monster
that almost ate Luke Skywalker in Return of

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:36.150
the Jedi?

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:40.660
Turns out that thing was from the planet Dathomir
— just like Darth Maul, along with a clan

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:43.210
of Force-wielding witches called the Nightsisters.

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:47.400
The animated Clone Wars TV show spells out
the details of Maul's upbringing, like the

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:51.690
fact that he was born to a high priestess
of the Nightsisters, grew up practicing Force

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:55.500
magic, and received a series of tattoos all
over his body.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.170
Some better than others.

00:00:57.170 --> 00:00:59.510
A Forceful family

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:04.720
During his early life on Dathomir, Maul had
two brothers: Feral and Savage Opress.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:09.510
After Maul left his homeworld with Darth Sidious,
both Feral and Savage Opress continued their

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:12.040
training, following in the traditions of their
tribe.

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:17.080
Eventually, Opress was chosen as a Sith apprentice
by the evil Asajj Ventress, one of the main

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:19.500
villains from the Clone Wars animated series.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.890
And how did Ventress test Opress's loyalty?

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:25.240
By commanding him to kill his brother, Feral.

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:29.300
"I said kill him."

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:30.320
"No"

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:34.740
If you think that test's bad, don't even ask
about the written exam.

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:39.190
Half-life

00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:43.860
When it comes to lightsaber fights, there
are cool, mysterious ways to die:

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:58.500
...and then there’s Darth Maul getting cut
in half.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:00.190
But it's hard to keep a good villain down.

00:02:00.190 --> 00:02:04.460
Despite being sliced in two, Darth Maul survived
his duel with Obi-Wan Kenobi.

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:09.159
Maul's tale of survival is detailed in The
Clone Wars-based comic book, The Sith Hunters.

00:02:09.159 --> 00:02:13.159
Using the same kind of hate-fueled Force power
that kept Darth Vader alive after getting

00:02:13.159 --> 00:02:18.379
carved up by Obi-Wan, Darth Maul's angry top-half
made his way to a garbage planet called Lotho

00:02:18.379 --> 00:02:19.379
Minor.

00:02:19.379 --> 00:02:24.049
There, he went crazy, became obsessed with
taking revenge on Obi-Wan — oh, and he figured

00:02:24.049 --> 00:02:26.700
out how to make a new set of robot-spider-legs.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:27.700
Like you do.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:31.950
Eventually, Maul's little brother, Savage
Opress, rescued him from Lotho Minor and brought

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:32.970
him back home.

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:37.599
There, Maul's mommy helped him find his lost
marbles, and even get a new pair of legs.

00:02:37.599 --> 00:02:39.139
"Magic legs"

00:02:39.139 --> 00:02:43.559
Fun fact: Darth Maul's original legs figured
out how to make a new robot torso, and has

00:02:43.559 --> 00:02:47.469
been washing dishes in Dexter Jettster's diner
ever since.

00:02:47.469 --> 00:02:48.719
Revenge of the Sith

00:02:48.719 --> 00:02:53.129
While raising hell around the galaxy, Darth
Maul and Savage Opress decided to go after

00:02:53.129 --> 00:02:58.609
not just Obi-Wan Kenobi, but also Maul's former
master: Darth Sidious, better known as Senator

00:02:58.609 --> 00:02:59.609
Palpatine.

00:02:59.609 --> 00:03:00.790
It didn't go super well for Maul, though.

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:05.239
Sidious managed to defeat the brothers, killing
Savage Opress, and imprisoning Maul for a

00:03:05.239 --> 00:03:06.239
time.

00:03:06.239 --> 00:03:09.959
Who would've guessed that confronting an all-powerful
master of the Dark Side of the Force who single-handedly

00:03:09.959 --> 00:03:14.299
engineered a galactic civil war and would
become the future emperor of evil space magic

00:03:14.299 --> 00:03:15.599
wouldn't be a great idea?

00:03:19.129 --> 00:03:20.129
Jedi trainer

00:03:20.129 --> 00:03:24.499
While The Clone Wars TV series may have ended,
the story was picked up again by the show

00:03:24.499 --> 00:03:25.909
Star Wars Rebels.

00:03:25.909 --> 00:03:29.480
That show follows the adventures of a group
of freedom fighters, including the Jedi and

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:32.489
Padawan pair of Kanan Jarrus and Ezra Bridger.

00:03:32.489 --> 00:03:36.540
And it was during season two that young Ezra
encountered Darth Maul, who taught him the

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:37.879
ways of the Dark Side.

00:03:37.879 --> 00:03:42.449
Fortunately for the fledgling Rebellion movement,
Maul's training didn't quite stick, and Ezra

00:03:42.449 --> 00:03:43.879
is still a good guy...for now.

00:03:43.879 --> 00:03:46.400
Man of few words

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:50.530
So now you know all about Darth Maul before
and after his debut in The Phantom Menace.

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:54.530
What you may not know, however, is that he's
actually barely in that movie at all, with

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:57.329
roughly 15 minutes of total screen time.

00:03:57.329 --> 00:04:01.709
And while his epic lightsaber duel with Obi-Wan
and Qui-Gon Jinn accounts for a good chunk

00:04:01.709 --> 00:04:04.980
of that, he still only uttered three actual
lines of dialogue.

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:09.109
Now, for your viewing pleasure, here are all
the lines spoken by one of the most legendary

00:04:09.109 --> 00:04:10.970
movie villains to get cut in half:

00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:16.340
"Tatooine is sparsely populated if the trace
was correct I will find them quickly master."

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:19.150
"At last we will reveal ourselves to the Jedi."

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:21.000
"At last we will have revenge."

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.660
"Yes my master"

00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:30.950
Needless to say, the end result didn't really
sit well with Peter Serafinowicz, the British

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:33.840
actor-comedian who was tapped to give Maul
his voice.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:37.840
Interestingly, he saw signs that maybe this
role wasn't all it was cracked up to be when

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:42.210
he first went in to record Maul's voice — and
shared the recording booth with George Lucas

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:43.210
himself:

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:47.840
"I said, how do you want me to do this.

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:49.990
What what direction can you give me.

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:52.800
He said just make him evil.

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:55.560
Just make him sound real evil.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:57.660
Alright, ok."

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:00.250
Darth Molly

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:04.510
When it comes to females, let's just say the
first six Star Wars movies didn't really,

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:06.000
well, have many of them.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:10.680
A couple of Princesses, a shapeshifting bounty
hunter with no backstory, and a handful of

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:15.060
aliens are just about the only women to show
up in George Lucas' Star Wars movies — which

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:18.780
makes it all the more interesting to learn
that there were briefly plans to make Darth

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:19.780
Maul a woman.

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:24.060
In the early days of pre-production for The
Phantom Menace, George Lucas reportedly explained

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:26.670
that Darth Maul would be "a figure from your
worst nightmare."

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:33.590
So, concept artist Iain McCaig drew just that:
an evil-looking Sith witch, streaked with

00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:35.000
bloody-looking ribbons.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:39.310
The concept evolved into Darth Maul from there,
but the makers of The Clone Wars television

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:43.240
show reportedly referred back to McCaig's
original "Sith witch" design for the creation

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:45.500
of Maul's mother, Talzin.

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:46.930
Darth Maul's future

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:50.950
It's hard to imagine that more than a decade
after he met his apparent demise in The Phantom

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:53.450
Menace that we'd have this much Darth Maul
to enjoy.

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:57.200
But his resurrection in the pages of Star
Wars comics and his continued relevance on

00:05:57.200 --> 00:06:01.090
the small screen means that this might still
be just the beginning for all things Maul.

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:05.280
With Star Wars Rebels continuing to feature
the horny, hateful Sith Lord, there's no telling

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:06.750
where he might show up next.

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:10.300
Could Darth Maul put in an appearance in Star
Wars: Episode VIII or IX?

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:14.271
And with spin-off movies starring Han Solo
and Lando Calrissian on the horizon, could

00:06:14.271 --> 00:06:17.930
we see a Darth Maul solo film sometime in
the not-so-distant future?

00:06:17.930 --> 00:06:21.740
It's hard to say now, but one thing is clear:
this is hardly the last we've seen of one

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:26.670
of Star Wars' most intimidating, enduring,
and enigmatic villains ever.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:32.100
"Handsome, Awesome.

00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:34.580
Awesome awesome and handsome.

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:37.060
Awesome.

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:41.680
I so awesome.

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:44.060
Was up weeze"

